# What this repository's em-dash scan leaves out, and why.
#
# One entry per line. An entry ending in / is a path prefix and covers every
# tracked path beneath it. Blank lines and lines whose first non-space character
# is # are ignored. Entries are read verbatim, so no leading or trailing space.
#
# THE TWO PREFIXES BELOW ARE THE VERBATIM BYTES OF A VENDORED PUBLICATION: 83
# files committed byte for byte so the shipped message-structure registry can be
# derived offline and audited. Exactly one of them,
# vendor/hl7-v2ig/message-structure/ACK-Scheduling.json, carries the JavaScript
# backslash-u spelling of the banned character inside HL7's own description text.
# There is no rewrite available. Editing a vendored byte forfeits the point of
# vendoring it, and dropping that structure would change what the registry
# derives. The ban is a rule about prose that people write, and these are
# grounded data rather than brand copy.
#
# THE EXCLUDED BYTES ARE NOT UNGUARDED. vendor/hl7-v2ig/snapshot.json records a
# sha256 for every one of the 83, and test/parser-structure-provenance.test.ts
# recomputes all 83 on every run, so a file edited to smuggle anything in reds
# the suite.
#
# THE EXCLUSION IS THESE TWO SUBDIRECTORIES AND NOTHING ELSE. This repository's
# own writing under vendor/ (README.md, snapshot.json) is still scanned, so
# nobody can put prose behind this exclusion by choosing a directory. Widening
# the set here is the move that would quietly weaken the gate: prefer rewriting
# the sentence with a period, a colon, a comma, or parentheses.
vendor/hl7-v2ig/message-structure/
vendor/hl7-v2ig/control-manifests/
